1
00:02:31,817 --> 00:02:34,337
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece

2
00:02:34,337 --> 00:02:37,257
must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

3
00:02:37,257 --> 00:02:41,617
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

4
00:02:41,617 --> 00:02:44,737
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber

5
00:02:44,737 --> 00:02:46,337
after eating the gum gum fruit,

6
00:02:46,337 --> 00:02:50,057
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

7
00:02:50,057 --> 00:02:52,977
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

8
00:02:56,977 --> 00:03:00,777
Two years have passed since the War of the Best in Marineford.

9
00:03:00,777 --> 00:03:04,617
Luffy and his crew reunite to continue on to the New World.

10
00:03:04,617 --> 00:03:06,897
Their first stop is Fishman Island,

11
00:03:06,897 --> 00:03:10,217
where they encounter King Neptune, Merman royalty,

12
00:03:10,217 --> 00:03:12,417
and conniving pirates alike.

13
00:03:12,417 --> 00:03:15,977
Soon, Luffy leaves on an adventure with the Mermaid Princess,

14
00:03:15,977 --> 00:03:19,017
leaving his crew to fend for themselves.

15
00:03:22,257 --> 00:03:26,097
40's Onslaught, the retaliatory plan set into motion!

16
00:03:30,777 --> 00:03:40,937
I've only read about them in books, of course,

17
00:03:40,937 --> 00:03:43,217
but doesn't it look just like a raccoon?

18
00:03:43,217 --> 00:03:47,897
Oh, yeah! That's funny! It's totally Chopper!

19
00:03:47,897 --> 00:03:51,017
Who's Chopper?

20
00:03:51,017 --> 00:03:54,857
Friend? Part of my crew? He's a doctor.

21
00:03:54,857 --> 00:03:57,017
I'm confused.

22
00:03:57,017 --> 00:03:59,017
Hmm.

23
00:03:59,017 --> 00:04:01,017
Are those giant flying fish?

24
00:04:03,017 --> 00:04:05,417
Thorneth? Too far away to tell!

25
00:04:05,417 --> 00:04:07,017
Is something wrong?

26
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:08,857
I can't see from in here!

27
00:04:11,817 --> 00:04:14,057
Mom, what are those weird fish?

28
00:04:14,057 --> 00:04:26,217
Whoa! Look at that!

29
00:04:26,217 --> 00:04:28,217
That's not horrible.

30
00:04:32,217 --> 00:04:35,017
Ryugu Palace! Ryugu Palace! Come in!

31
00:04:35,017 --> 00:04:37,337
This is Border Control. Come in!

32
00:04:37,337 --> 00:04:38,777
Can anyone hear me?

33
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:41,017
Hello? Hello?

34
00:04:42,137 --> 00:04:43,097
I wonder what's wrong.

35
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:46,217
I'm still not getting anything at all.

36
00:04:47,337 --> 00:04:48,537
You think the snail's sick?

37
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:52,217
There's no immediate call for alarm,

38
00:04:52,217 --> 00:04:54,617
but it does seem like there are a lot of people coming in

39
00:04:54,617 --> 00:04:55,977
from the fish man district.

40
00:04:55,977 --> 00:04:56,697
It worries me.

41
00:04:57,337 --> 00:05:00,137
That many wouldn't come at one time just for shopping.

42
00:05:00,137 --> 00:05:02,377
They're dangerous people. Anything could happen.

43
00:05:08,777 --> 00:05:10,377
I don't know.

44
00:05:22,537 --> 00:05:23,897
Today is the day.

45
00:05:24,857 --> 00:05:26,217
History will be made.

46
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:30,057
All of Fishman Island will be united under one flag.

47
00:05:30,697 --> 00:05:34,537
Mermaids, mermen, and fishmen must all come together.

48
00:05:34,537 --> 00:05:36,537
We must all be of the same mind.

49
00:05:37,417 --> 00:05:39,177
We've tolerated humans long enough.

50
00:05:39,737 --> 00:05:41,737
Land dwellers are inferior.

51
00:05:41,737 --> 00:05:44,537
We will rule them, or they will die.

52
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,577
We will erase the mistakes of the past

53
00:05:53,577 --> 00:05:55,737
and forge an everlasting legacy.

54
00:05:55,737 --> 00:05:58,617
Yeah!

55
00:05:58,617 --> 00:06:00,457
Ah, ho, ho, ho.

56
00:06:00,457 --> 00:06:04,777
Today is the anniversary of our engagement, dear Shirahoshi.

57
00:06:04,777 --> 00:06:06,297
But it's no rush.

58
00:06:06,297 --> 00:06:08,057
We don't have to get married today.

59
00:06:08,057 --> 00:06:09,737
I'll wait until tomorrow.

60
00:06:09,737 --> 00:06:13,337
Seems the Sun Pirates and Jinbei have decided not to join us.

61
00:06:13,337 --> 00:06:16,377
Annoying, but it isn't exactly unexpected.

62
00:06:16,377 --> 00:06:17,737
We take down Neptune.

63
00:06:17,737 --> 00:06:19,257
We take down Fukuboshi.

64
00:06:19,257 --> 00:06:20,217
Ryuboshi.

65
00:06:20,217 --> 00:06:20,857
Momboshi.

66
00:06:20,857 --> 00:06:26,857
Then his army will fall, assuming they don't surrender first.

67
00:06:28,857 --> 00:06:30,777
But that's no fun.

68
00:06:30,777 --> 00:06:32,617
I want to feast on their flesh.

69
00:06:32,617 --> 00:06:36,137
You tell me what to cut, and then I'll cut it.

70
00:06:38,217 --> 00:06:39,977
You know the plan, right?

71
00:06:39,977 --> 00:06:43,257
We split up, conquer one area, and move on.

72
00:06:43,257 --> 00:06:44,937
They won't know what hit them.

73
00:06:44,937 --> 00:06:58,937
Before this day is done, the Ryugu Kingdom will fall, and we will reign!

74
00:07:05,737 --> 00:07:06,457
Good.

75
00:07:06,457 --> 00:07:07,177
Right on time.

76
00:07:09,817 --> 00:07:10,937
The sea forest, huh?

77
00:07:11,657 --> 00:07:13,097
I wonder what that's like.

78
00:07:13,817 --> 00:07:16,137
That's Nico Robin of the Straw Hats.

79
00:07:16,137 --> 00:07:17,017
No question.

80
00:07:22,937 --> 00:07:23,977
Don't move!

81
00:07:23,977 --> 00:07:27,257
You and your crewmates are suspects in two investigations.

82
00:07:27,897 --> 00:07:31,017
First off, we have a missing person case.

83
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:32,217
Or people, rather.

84
00:07:32,857 --> 00:07:35,817
Mermaids that your crew had recent contact with.

85
00:07:35,817 --> 00:07:40,537
Second, a powerful psychic has named you as a risk to the safety of our island.

86
00:07:40,537 --> 00:07:42,537
We can't afford to take any chances.

87
00:07:43,097 --> 00:07:44,777
So we're arresting your crew!

88
00:07:46,457 --> 00:07:49,657
I'm sorry, but I have no idea what you're talking about.

89
00:07:49,657 --> 00:07:51,337
So you're here because of a psychic?

90
00:07:52,537 --> 00:07:55,577
That doesn't sound very scientific or sensible.

91
00:07:55,577 --> 00:07:58,937
I'm disappointed your culture still puts faith in such nonsense.

92
00:07:59,977 --> 00:08:02,137
Madam Charlie's premonitions are never wrong!

93
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,457
Now shut up and come with us!

94
00:08:04,457 --> 00:08:05,737
I think I'll pass.

95
00:08:06,377 --> 00:08:08,217
Wouldn't want to miss my bus after all.

96
00:08:09,177 --> 00:08:10,297
Capture her!

97
00:08:15,177 --> 00:08:16,297
Now, Mille Flux!

98
00:08:16,297 --> 00:08:31,017
If anyone can move.

99
00:08:31,017 --> 00:08:33,017
Try to stop her.

100
00:08:33,017 --> 00:08:45,657
It seems my theory was correct.

101
00:08:46,297 --> 00:08:48,137
There's a poneglyph hidden here somewhere.

102
00:08:48,857 --> 00:08:50,537
The crew can take care of themselves.

103
00:08:51,257 --> 00:09:01,737
I can't miss a chance to uncover the world's lost history.

104
00:09:01,737 --> 00:09:15,497
But you give it up already?

105
00:09:15,497 --> 00:09:16,857
They're terribly persistent.

106
00:09:18,937 --> 00:09:20,217
How'd it come to this?

107
00:09:20,217 --> 00:09:22,617
We were supposed to have a banquet, weren't we?

108
00:09:22,617 --> 00:09:25,577
I got to drink some booze and now I get to fight.

109
00:09:25,577 --> 00:09:27,897
I don't see anything to complain about here.

110
00:09:27,897 --> 00:09:30,617
If they want to start trouble with us, then fine.

111
00:09:30,617 --> 00:09:32,297
That's what they're gonna get.

112
00:09:32,297 --> 00:09:33,977
Come on, give me a break.

113
00:09:33,977 --> 00:09:35,417
I know you like to be a tough guy,

114
00:09:35,417 --> 00:09:37,657
but don't you think we've got enough trouble already?

115
00:09:37,657 --> 00:09:40,937
Nobody cares if pirates fight other pirates, all right?

116
00:09:40,937 --> 00:09:42,697
It's fine as long as we win.

117
00:09:42,697 --> 00:09:43,817
Any excuse, huh?

118
00:09:43,817 --> 00:09:45,257
Geez, why do I even bother?

119
00:09:45,977 --> 00:09:47,257
What's the deal?

120
00:09:47,257 --> 00:09:50,377
You keep coming at us, but you're barely even alive!

121
00:09:50,377 --> 00:09:53,177
Can't we settle this peacefully before someone dies?

122
00:09:53,177 --> 00:09:54,617
They won't listen to reason.

123
00:09:54,617 --> 00:09:55,657
Let's just end this.

124
00:10:02,057 --> 00:10:03,977
Just pass them and hit the switch.

125
00:10:03,977 --> 00:10:05,177
I know we can make it.

126
00:10:05,737 --> 00:10:09,017
All we have to do is open the gate and they'll let us live.

127
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:13,097
Sorry, Straw Hats, but you're finished.

128
00:10:13,097 --> 00:10:14,137
Time to die!

129
00:10:18,617 --> 00:10:19,897
Screaming, how fun!

130
00:10:19,897 --> 00:10:22,057
No mercy!

131
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:24,937
Come here!

132
00:10:32,217 --> 00:10:34,137
I'm afraid you leave me no choice.

133
00:10:44,617 --> 00:10:46,217
You're not gonna beat us, you guys.

134
00:10:46,217 --> 00:10:47,017
Move it!

135
00:10:49,897 --> 00:10:56,697
I'm still thinking about those huge fish.

136
00:10:57,337 --> 00:11:00,777
Luffy, how did you get so strong?

137
00:11:00,777 --> 00:11:02,857
You weren't born that way, were you?

138
00:11:02,857 --> 00:11:05,017
No, but I've been training since I was real little.

139
00:11:05,017 --> 00:11:08,377
I don't have to, because there's always somebody stronger.

140
00:11:08,377 --> 00:11:11,737
Wow, someone stronger than you?

141
00:11:11,737 --> 00:11:12,457
That can't be.

142
00:11:14,457 --> 00:11:15,817
What's wrong, Shark?

143
00:11:15,817 --> 00:11:16,937
Don't tell me you're sick.

144
00:11:16,937 --> 00:11:19,097
Megalo?

145
00:11:19,097 --> 00:11:20,457
You're acting weird.

146
00:11:20,457 --> 00:11:21,897
Do you need to take a break?

147
00:11:27,657 --> 00:11:29,817
Oh man, that was a close one.

148
00:11:29,817 --> 00:11:31,497
You gotta be more careful, Shark.

149
00:11:31,497 --> 00:11:35,657
So what if I enjoyed it?

150
00:11:35,657 --> 00:11:37,257
I fought him because I had to.

151
00:11:37,257 --> 00:11:40,137
I see, then you are a bloodthirsty butcher.

152
00:11:40,137 --> 00:11:42,937
You'll turn your blade on us next, won't you?

153
00:11:42,937 --> 00:11:46,377
Look, these guys were after our heads, and probably yours too.

154
00:11:46,377 --> 00:11:48,137
Did you expect us to serve them tea?

155
00:11:48,937 --> 00:11:50,057
Good idea.

156
00:11:50,057 --> 00:11:52,377
That sounds like a lovely way to settle things.

157
00:11:52,377 --> 00:11:54,297
Oh yeah, I'm sure they would go for that.

158
00:11:54,297 --> 00:11:55,577
Who can say?

159
00:11:55,577 --> 00:12:00,377
Certainly not them right now, since you knocked them out before we could learn why they were here.

160
00:12:01,337 --> 00:12:04,937
Except it doesn't matter what they wanted because we stopped them from doing it.

161
00:12:04,937 --> 00:12:06,377
Man, I hate this.

162
00:12:06,377 --> 00:12:08,617
How do we turn into the bad guys?

163
00:12:08,617 --> 00:12:11,977
It's because everyone on our crew is so irresponsible.

164
00:12:11,977 --> 00:12:13,337
Or just plain violent.

165
00:12:13,977 --> 00:12:16,137
Well, just look at our captain.

166
00:12:16,137 --> 00:12:16,537
Good point.

167
00:12:16,537 --> 00:12:18,697
Too late for regrets now.

168
00:12:20,857 --> 00:12:24,457
Speaking of Luffy, I wonder if he came across the mermaid princess.

169
00:12:24,457 --> 00:12:26,057
I'd still quite like to meet her.

170
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:30,057
My poor little girl.

171
00:12:30,057 --> 00:12:31,337
You fiends.

172
00:12:31,337 --> 00:12:33,337
What have you done to her wife?

173
00:12:33,337 --> 00:12:34,617
Stop crying.

174
00:12:34,617 --> 00:12:38,137
I know we tied up your guards, but we didn't lay a finger on your daughter.

175
00:12:38,137 --> 00:12:39,257
Liar.

176
00:12:39,257 --> 00:12:42,777
Straw Hat Luffy took her away, my sweet princess.

177
00:12:42,777 --> 00:12:44,937
I can assure you that's not the case.

178
00:12:44,937 --> 00:12:47,657
I only saw Luffy and Mr. Shark leave the room.

179
00:12:47,657 --> 00:12:50,937
Surely I would have noticed if they had a mermaid princess with them.

180
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:53,097
If you knew her, you would understand.

181
00:12:53,097 --> 00:12:55,577
She would never sneak out on her own.

182
00:12:55,577 --> 00:12:58,937
Also, someone would notice if she simply squam out of the room.

183
00:12:58,937 --> 00:13:01,337
She takes after me when it comes to size.

184
00:13:02,457 --> 00:13:03,897
Your daughter's as big as you?

185
00:13:04,937 --> 00:13:06,057
De Montpourri!

186
00:13:08,297 --> 00:13:09,417
Oh, thank you.

187
00:13:10,057 --> 00:13:11,977
Why did I realize it sooner?

188
00:13:11,977 --> 00:13:15,017
Straw Hat hid Shirahoshi inside Megalo's mouth,

189
00:13:15,017 --> 00:13:16,937
and they all left the palace together.

190
00:13:20,937 --> 00:13:21,897
Come on, your highness.

191
00:13:21,897 --> 00:13:23,897
You shouldn't joke at a time like this.

192
00:13:23,897 --> 00:13:25,017
That's crazy.

193
00:13:25,017 --> 00:13:27,337
I know Straw Hat has a wild reputation,

194
00:13:27,337 --> 00:13:29,337
but that's pretty far out there, even for him.

195
00:13:39,497 --> 00:13:40,297
Dang it, Shark.

196
00:13:40,297 --> 00:13:41,657
You got me sneezing now.

197
00:13:42,457 --> 00:13:44,057
Sharks make you sneeze?

198
00:13:44,057 --> 00:13:45,097
I didn't know that.

199
00:13:45,097 --> 00:13:47,657
They don't, but sometimes I sneeze out of nowhere.

200
00:13:48,937 --> 00:13:49,737
Wonder why.

201
00:13:49,737 --> 00:14:06,217
Come back, Shirahoshi!

202
00:14:06,217 --> 00:14:09,097
That's enough.

203
00:14:09,097 --> 00:14:12,057
Luffy may be a pirate, but he's not a kidnapper.

204
00:14:12,057 --> 00:14:14,217
There has to be another culprit out there.

205
00:14:14,217 --> 00:14:16,137
You can't talk your way out of this one.

206
00:14:16,137 --> 00:14:18,777
If my little girl doesn't come back safe,

207
00:14:18,777 --> 00:14:20,457
then I'm keeping your ship,

208
00:14:20,457 --> 00:14:23,657
and I'll be keeping your friends in jail.

209
00:14:23,657 --> 00:14:24,777
No fear.

210
00:14:24,777 --> 00:14:26,057
We're victims here too.

211
00:14:26,057 --> 00:14:37,017
I did it.

212
00:14:41,017 --> 00:14:42,777
Looks like they finished their job.

213
00:14:42,777 --> 00:14:45,257
Not bad for a bunch of humans.

214
00:14:54,697 --> 00:14:56,777
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

215
00:14:56,777 --> 00:14:57,657
Hey, Sonny.

216
00:14:57,657 --> 00:14:58,697
Looking good.

217
00:14:58,697 --> 00:15:00,297
Things got pretty wild back there,

218
00:15:00,297 --> 00:15:02,937
but you can't keep a super ship down.

219
00:15:02,937 --> 00:15:06,777
As you can see, others weren't so lucky.

220
00:15:07,337 --> 00:15:10,377
The tide brings many sunken vessels to this spot.

221
00:15:10,377 --> 00:15:13,897
It's almost like a graveyard for ships that couldn't reach the new world.

222
00:15:14,617 --> 00:15:17,177
And yet this is a place overflowing with life.

223
00:15:17,897 --> 00:15:20,457
Thanks to the grace of the Sun Tree Eve,

224
00:15:20,457 --> 00:15:23,017
many colorful fish and coral make their home here.

225
00:15:23,017 --> 00:15:24,857
And whales too, huh?

226
00:15:24,857 --> 00:15:27,737
I don't think I've ever seen so many in one place before.

227
00:15:27,737 --> 00:15:29,577
Some of them are even bigger than the Sunny.

228
00:15:30,537 --> 00:15:32,617
Even if they're tucked away in deep waters,

229
00:15:33,177 --> 00:15:35,577
whales always know where fertile seas lie.

230
00:15:38,377 --> 00:15:40,377
This place is a real wonderland.

231
00:15:43,177 --> 00:15:45,257
It's endlessly fascinating.

232
00:15:45,257 --> 00:15:48,617
No matter how much I observe, there's always something new to find.

233
00:15:49,497 --> 00:15:50,617
So it's not just me.

234
00:15:51,337 --> 00:15:54,137
Even the people who live down here think this place is a miracle.

235
00:15:54,137 --> 00:15:56,217
All of Fishman Island, I mean.

236
00:16:00,057 --> 00:16:02,377
I don't know how you got wood from the Tree of Adam,

237
00:16:02,377 --> 00:16:05,417
but this is a fine ship, worthy of its parts.

238
00:16:05,417 --> 00:16:07,817
Damn straight. This is my masterpiece.

239
00:16:07,817 --> 00:16:10,857
Tom made a ship out of the same stuff for Gold Roger.

240
00:16:10,857 --> 00:16:13,177
So nothing less will do for my captain.

241
00:16:15,337 --> 00:16:17,337
I'll do the ship coding for you.

242
00:16:17,337 --> 00:16:18,857
And I'll do it with gusto.

243
00:16:20,297 --> 00:16:21,817
Haven't heard that one in a while.

244
00:16:21,817 --> 00:16:24,857
Oh, uh, sorry. I never caught your name.

245
00:16:24,857 --> 00:16:26,297
Call me Den.

246
00:16:26,297 --> 00:16:27,737
So, Den.

247
00:16:27,737 --> 00:16:32,777
Don't take this the wrong way, but for being his brother, you sure don't look much like Tom.

248
00:16:32,777 --> 00:16:35,497
I mean, you're a merman and he was a fish man.

249
00:16:35,497 --> 00:16:37,097
Was one of you adopted or something?

250
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:41,177
That's a human-centric way to think.

251
00:16:42,217 --> 00:16:46,377
I can't hardly blame you, since family members tend to look so much alike on the surface.

252
00:16:47,337 --> 00:16:49,097
It works a bit differently with us.

253
00:16:49,977 --> 00:16:53,817
We carry genes from our ancestors that can show up in different ways.

254
00:16:53,817 --> 00:16:56,537
And this rule applies to both merfolk and fish men.

255
00:16:57,257 --> 00:17:01,737
So, if an octopus mermaid gives birth to a shark merman, that's normal.

256
00:17:02,377 --> 00:17:06,937
It just means that she, or the father, has shark mermans somewhere in their lineage.

257
00:17:07,657 --> 00:17:13,337
The bottom line is, nothing really surprises us, no matter what way our children turn out.

258
00:17:13,337 --> 00:17:19,817
That's why it doesn't make much sense to us when humans discriminate against someone just because they look a certain way.

259
00:17:20,457 --> 00:17:23,897
See, the way you look doesn't say a thing about who you are.

260
00:17:27,657 --> 00:17:31,497
Speaking of which, was one of your ancestors a robot, perhaps?

261
00:17:31,497 --> 00:17:33,177
That's not how it works, bro.

262
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:33,897
My mistake.

263
00:17:34,777 --> 00:17:37,577
You're human, so one of your parents was a robot?

264
00:17:37,577 --> 00:17:38,857
How does that make sense?

265
00:17:39,497 --> 00:17:40,617
You tell me.

266
00:17:40,617 --> 00:17:42,377
It was a rhetorical question.

267
00:17:42,937 --> 00:17:46,297
I should have said, I got a letter from Granny Kokoro.

268
00:17:46,297 --> 00:17:48,777
So I heard all about you and Iceberg.

269
00:17:48,777 --> 00:17:50,937
You and the old bag stay in touch?

270
00:17:50,937 --> 00:17:51,657
That's nice.

271
00:17:52,457 --> 00:17:55,337
Now that is one face I never thought I'd miss.

272
00:17:55,337 --> 00:17:58,617
At any rate, I heard the whole story, the good and the bad.

273
00:17:59,897 --> 00:18:04,457
I know that my brother died the very same way he lived, with gusto.

274
00:18:05,257 --> 00:18:08,697
Well, either way, I do appreciate you coming here to tell me.

275
00:18:08,697 --> 00:18:10,617
It seems he chose his students well.

276
00:18:13,657 --> 00:18:15,177
Aw, you're flattering me.

277
00:18:16,537 --> 00:18:18,217
Are you sure you're not a robot?

278
00:18:19,497 --> 00:18:21,577
Well, it's complicated.

279
00:18:21,577 --> 00:18:23,177
Let's drop it, okay?

280
00:18:23,177 --> 00:18:25,337
By the way, I've been meaning to ask you.

281
00:18:25,337 --> 00:18:27,417
There's a dude sitting all alone over there.

282
00:18:27,417 --> 00:18:28,297
Do you know who he is?

283
00:18:30,137 --> 00:18:30,537
Uh-huh.

284
00:18:31,577 --> 00:18:33,257
That would be the boss, Jinbei.

285
00:18:33,257 --> 00:18:34,137
Huh?

286
00:18:34,137 --> 00:18:34,937
Boss of what?

287
00:18:35,737 --> 00:18:37,817
Consider it a term of endearment.

288
00:18:37,817 --> 00:18:39,577
He's waiting for someone.

289
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:41,737
But he doesn't want to enter the island.

290
00:18:41,737 --> 00:18:43,177
Because he's a wanted man.

291
00:18:43,177 --> 00:18:43,737
Ah!

292
00:18:59,737 --> 00:19:00,857
Intruder alert!

293
00:19:00,857 --> 00:19:03,337
But the front gate!

294
00:19:03,337 --> 00:19:05,497
How did you scoundrels get in here?

295
00:19:07,497 --> 00:19:09,257
Well, isn't this convenient?

296
00:19:09,257 --> 00:19:12,217
I was ready for a fight, but everyone's tied up.

297
00:19:12,217 --> 00:19:15,337
I didn't expect much from those pirates we sent.

298
00:19:15,337 --> 00:19:17,657
Don't tell me they're the ones who did this.

299
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,257
It doesn't matter.

300
00:19:19,257 --> 00:19:20,377
It doesn't matter.

301
00:19:20,377 --> 00:19:23,017
If someone leaves you a present, you don't ask questions.

302
00:19:24,377 --> 00:19:25,417
They look scared.

303
00:19:25,417 --> 00:19:29,897
I know you.

304
00:19:29,897 --> 00:19:32,057
What's he doing here?

305
00:19:32,057 --> 00:19:37,257
We fought so hard to keep Vanderdaken away, and now he wants us right in.

306
00:19:38,057 --> 00:19:39,577
And is that who I think it is?

307
00:19:42,057 --> 00:19:44,617
Hordy Jones from the Fishman District?

308
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:47,177
What does he want?

309
00:19:47,177 --> 00:19:48,377
This can't be good.

310
00:19:48,377 --> 00:19:49,257
Hordy.

311
00:19:49,257 --> 00:19:49,897
Hordy.

312
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:51,097
I know that name.

313
00:19:53,417 --> 00:19:55,097
He once served us.

314
00:19:55,097 --> 00:19:58,617
That is, he was a decorated soldier in the Royal Army.

315
00:20:05,657 --> 00:20:10,057
Actually, on second thought, are you setting a trap for us?

316
00:20:10,057 --> 00:20:12,297
Had an awful lot of visitors today, huh?

317
00:20:15,097 --> 00:20:16,617
They're not like the last batch.

318
00:20:17,177 --> 00:20:18,457
You did this.

319
00:20:18,457 --> 00:20:20,137
You must be accomplices.

320
00:20:20,137 --> 00:20:21,097
Just admit it.

321
00:20:21,097 --> 00:20:22,537
You let them into the palace.

322
00:20:22,537 --> 00:20:23,497
Oh, really?

323
00:20:23,497 --> 00:20:24,537
It's our fault?

324
00:20:24,537 --> 00:20:28,697
You realize we wouldn't even be here in the first place if your king hadn't invited us?

325
00:20:28,697 --> 00:20:30,217
I don't know those guys.

326
00:20:30,217 --> 00:20:31,497
I don't want to.

327
00:20:31,497 --> 00:20:32,297
They're scary.

328
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:35,497
Hey, you gotta give our weapons back.

329
00:20:35,497 --> 00:20:36,537
This is bad.

330
00:20:36,537 --> 00:20:38,297
We're gonna need to fight them.

331
00:20:38,297 --> 00:20:39,897
Vanderdaken.

332
00:20:39,897 --> 00:20:41,817
So you're the one behind this.

333
00:20:41,817 --> 00:20:43,497
Straw Hat was innocent.

334
00:20:44,217 --> 00:20:45,737
Give me back my daughter.

335
00:20:45,737 --> 00:20:47,177
You've made her suffer enough.

336
00:20:47,177 --> 00:20:54,137
All father-in-laws say that, but you'll come around by the time our honeymoon is over.

337
00:20:54,137 --> 00:20:55,737
This, I suspect.

338
00:20:55,737 --> 00:20:58,057
I'll never be your father-in-law.

339
00:20:58,057 --> 00:21:01,817
Now, where did you take Shirahoshi if you harmed one hair on her head?

340
00:21:01,817 --> 00:21:03,657
You're losing your mind, old man.

341
00:21:04,457 --> 00:21:07,737
If I already had her, why would I bother breaking in here?

342
00:21:07,737 --> 00:21:09,497
Don't play dumb with me.

343
00:21:09,497 --> 00:21:11,337
You're here and my daughter is missing.

344
00:21:11,337 --> 00:21:12,697
The situation is clear.

345
00:21:12,697 --> 00:21:15,657
Someone took my Shirahoshi?

346
00:21:15,657 --> 00:21:17,497
Ah, this is a tragedy.

347
00:21:18,617 --> 00:21:21,897
She's not yours, and damn right it's a tragedy.

348
00:21:21,897 --> 00:21:23,257
Calm down, your highness.

349
00:21:23,257 --> 00:21:26,697
This is going nowhere, and we need answers quickly.

350
00:21:31,817 --> 00:21:33,097
Enough screaming.

351
00:21:33,097 --> 00:21:33,897
It's a bluff.

352
00:21:34,777 --> 00:21:35,817
See this?

353
00:21:35,817 --> 00:21:38,777
All the pirates you threw at her are here in the palace.

354
00:21:38,777 --> 00:21:40,377
That means she must be close.

355
00:21:41,097 --> 00:21:45,817
Even if Neptune is telling the truth and she's gone, she couldn't have gotten far.

356
00:21:45,817 --> 00:21:47,577
Somebody help me?

357
00:21:47,577 --> 00:21:52,057
Besides, one little toss and you can track her down anywhere.

358
00:21:52,057 --> 00:21:56,937
Don't tell me love has made you so blind that you forgot how to use your own power.

359
00:22:00,857 --> 00:22:02,857
His power? What's that?

360
00:22:02,857 --> 00:22:04,057
Good idea.

361
00:22:04,057 --> 00:22:09,577
You know, Hardy, for a muscle head, you're really pretty clever when it comes down to it.

362
00:22:09,577 --> 00:22:11,017
Huh? Now he's leaving?

363
00:22:11,017 --> 00:22:13,737
I have a real bad feeling about this.

364
00:22:15,817 --> 00:22:24,057
All right, Mr. Coral. Find my princess for me!

365
00:22:28,377 --> 00:22:30,537
Oh! It is flying away!

366
00:22:34,537 --> 00:22:36,617
We've been in love for ten years!

367
00:22:36,617 --> 00:22:39,097
Nothing can tear us apart, princess!

368
00:22:39,097 --> 00:22:41,017
Except death, that is!

369
00:22:41,657 --> 00:22:44,697
And then, I had a real big fart!

370
00:22:45,817 --> 00:22:48,617
That is funny!

371
00:22:49,257 --> 00:22:51,257
But it's a bit inappropriate, too.

372
00:22:51,257 --> 00:22:52,457
Oh, oops!

373
00:22:56,057 --> 00:22:58,937
If I can't have you, then nobody can!

374
00:22:58,937 --> 00:23:02,777
You're about to be a big beautiful corpse, Sarah Jose!

375
00:23:02,777 --> 00:23:04,217
Hey!

376
00:23:08,217 --> 00:23:13,017
As seawater pours through the palace's broken wall, Hordy attacks Neptune's army.

377
00:23:13,017 --> 00:23:17,097
Neptune risks his life to protect his soldiers, but cannot triumph in battle.

378
00:23:17,097 --> 00:23:21,337
Just when things are starting to look grim, Zoro challenges Hordy himself.

379
00:23:21,337 --> 00:23:27,657
However, with the seawater continuing to rise, the swordsman is forced to battle the fishman underwater.

380
00:23:27,657 --> 00:23:29,577
On the next, One Piece!

381
00:23:29,577 --> 00:23:31,577
The Battle in the Ryugu Palace!

382
00:23:31,577 --> 00:23:33,177
Zoro versus Hordy!

383
00:23:33,177 --> 00:23:35,337
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

384
00:23:35,337 --> 00:23:36,817
Yes!

385
00:23:40,657 --> 00:23:41,137
One Piece!

386
00:23:41,657 --> 00:23:43,657
I'm gonna be king of the 누� octa.

387
00:23:43,657 --> 00:23:44,657
домойendo!

388
00:23:44,657 --> 00:23:52,277
New to the

389
00:23:52,697 --> 00:23:53,577
Guru!", Michael!

